extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 112-115 (cache p113-p116, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. The entry heading Police: TRG O.C.C. (also known as Special Ops: Tactical Response Group) and the start of its lore are at the foot of printed 112; printed 113 (cache p114) is a full page illustration; the rest of the lore, the TRG O.C.C. Bonuses and the stat block as far as the Science line are on printed 114; the stat block ends with Money, Rank and Cybernetics on printed 115. || HEADING: no NPC or villain heading, so no evil tag. It is listed under Optional City O.C.C.s on printed 105, which has no men-at-arms heading; occ_group men-of-arms is a reading of the class as an armed service. The class prints its own Base S.D.C. (4D6 plus O.C.C. and skill bonuses), so no men_of_arms line is needed. || XP: the City Administrator, Cyber-Specter, Police TRG ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render. || BONUSES (ability 1): the 1D6+12 S.D.C. bonus is a pool bonus; +3 initiative, +1 disarm, +4 pull punch, +4 vs Horror Factor stored. +2 to save vs illusion and mind control is stored as mind_control 2 and a saves.other entry labelled vs illusions. (Ability 2): +1 M.E., +1 P.P., +2 P.E. and +1D6+4 Spd stored. || SPECIAL WEAPONS TRAINING (ability 4): a choice of two, stored as skills.mos with choose 1. Power armor is printed as Pilot: Robots & Power Armors, focusing on three different Power Armor suits with training in Robot Power Armor Elite; stored as Robots & Power Armor at the catalog base and the general Robot Combat Elite row once, with the three suits in the note, because the catalog''s suit-specific Elite rows are other books'' suits. Heavy Weapons is Demolitions, Demolitions Disposal, Underwater Demolitions and Basic Electronics, all at +13%, plus Sniper and W.P. Heavy Weapons (the catalog row W.P. Heavy Military Weapons). The one extra attack per melee when using heavy weapons is conditional and is a special_abilities entry, not a bonus. || SKILLS: Speaks English at 97% is Language: Australian English at 97 with no per-level gain. Literacy (+30%) is Literacy: Native Language at 70. Surveillance Systems is Surveillance. Pilot: Hovercycle and Pilot: Jet Pack are the rows Hovercycles, Skycycles & Rocket Bikes and Jet Packs. W.P. Automatic Rifle is W.P. Automatic and Semi-automatic Rifles. Hand to Hand: Expert can become Martial Arts or Assassin for one related skill; the book states no alignment condition for Assassin. || RELATED: two from Military or Espionage and four others are stored as count 6 with one floor of two. The book prints two separate later tracks: one additional W.P. at levels 2, 4, 8 and 12, and one additional skill limited to Espionage, Military and Technical at levels 2, 5, 9 and 13. Both are stored in one schedule (two picks at level 2, one at 4, 5, 8, 9, 12 and 13); the schedule cannot restrict a pick to a category, so the W.P.-only and the three-category limits are in the note and are not enforced. Electrical Basic only is Basic Electronics. Cowboy, Rogue, Science and Wilderness are printed None and left out. || MONEY: 1D6x1000 dollars in personal savings stored (printed lD6x$1000; Australian dollars equal credits). The monthly salary of 3,000 rising 400 per level and the discounts are in GM Notes. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: badge and identification have no row; web harness and utility belt are stored as the one utility-belt row; the headset radio and notebook computer use the nearest catalog rows. The M.D. sidearm is stored as the NeraTech M-01 and the M.D. rifle as the generic weapon row. The vehicles a TRG agent can be issued (patrol cruiser, jet pack, hovercycle, light assault APC, Security Commando powered armor) and the standing power armor of an operative with that training are in GM Notes. || NOT STORED: Rank (starts as a Corporal) is in GM Notes. The squad make-up and the one in eight who is a major or master psychic are background."
